bug_descriptions |bug_id, line_num, content|
    seed_jit_len_bound_proof_accepts_non_array_receiver_2026-11-27, 0, "Repro (seed c3f521ba19bf8db2 = hoisted-generic-get, release/1.0.0, aarch64, JIT; interpreter correct): fn main() -> i64: val t = (7, 40, 3); var s = 0; val n = t.len(); var i: u64 = 0; while i < n: s = s * 100 + t[i]; i = i + 1 hangs (timeout; interpreter 74003); with var i = 0 the JIT returns 0. Two defects: (1) array_local_for_len_expr (src/compiler_rust/compiler/src/mir/lower/lowering_core.rs:598) accepted any .len() receiver, so a tuple or text local got the bound proof and a loop preheader that calls rt_array_data_ptr / rt_array_is_byte_packed on a non-array, and the tuple arm of lower_index_expr passed the hoisted pointer to rt_tuple_get. (2) A tuple .len() had no HIR result type and lowered to the undefined Tuple.len, which the JIT answered with -1 (print gave <value:0xffffffffffffffff>; a u64 counter against it never ends). A text local loop (val t = \"abc\") read correctly but still hoisted rt_array_data_ptr from the string. Found in review of 0ec41b497be (Fable)."

