bug_investigation_logs |bug_id, line_num, content|
    seed_jit_len_bound_proof_accepts_non_array_receiver_2026-11-27, 1, "2026-11-27 opus-bugbatch fix. (1) array_local_for_len_expr now admits only a receiver whose type is HirType::Array, so tuple / text locals get no bound proof and no rt_array_data_ptr preheader (tuple arm of lower_index_expr can no longer see a hoisted pointer). (2) HIR types a tuple .len() as i64 and MIR lowers it to rt_tuple_len (was the undefined Tuple.len, -1). Red->green: compiler/tests/seed_jit_len_bound_proof_non_array.rs: tuple len -1 -> 3; u64 tuple loop timeout -> 74003; text loop 13; i64-counter tuple loop 0 -> 50 (red with only the HIR change reverted); MIR for tuple / text loops has no rt_array_data_ptr. e2e on seed 20ce479a53519bab: tuple/text loops (u64 and i64 counters) and printed t.len() match the interpreter. Perf vs parent 0ec41b497be, 3 alternated rounds, 1e9 reads: hoisted [u32] best 1.38 vs 1.37 s, hoisted [u64] 1.76 vs 1.76 s, RSS 41 MB: no regression; both typed loops still hoist (MIR has _data_at / _raw_data_at). Also covered the untested runtime trap sites u32_push_known_at, u32/u64_push_known_data_at (child-process test, exit 1 + PANIC line). Compiler lib: 12 origin failures + the order-dependent seed_builtin_discriminants_are_the_declared_ordinal."

